snippet.textDisplay:
@vajona3894 AI is the name of a field of computer science that's existed since the 1950s (and I know this first hand). So, you're trying to redefine the term so that only AGI counts as AI, then declaring AI doesn't exist. That's a semantic argument, not a technical one.

And, as I said, nothing operates outside its underlying rules. Machine learning systems aren't explicitly programmed with every behavior they exhibit. They learn statistical relationships from data and generalize to novel inputs, much as humans learn from experience rather than being born with every behavior explicitly specified.

But hey, keep trying to warp reality to your delusions, actually acting childish.

