snippet.textDisplay:
@nguyenvuminhkhoi8179 What are you talking about? Isn't this exactly where robotics is needed? As people grow old, they need a robot that can be on standby 24/7 to care for them. Repetitive and heavy work can also be replaced by robots. Even an inexpensive robot combined with a perfect AI database would greatly alleviate the shortage of medical resources. Imagine every village having a top‑tier surgeon and the most extensive AI diagnostic database—ordinary doctors would also be freed from exhausting work and become consultants and online guides. This is a foreseeable future.

Besides, although you seem to know something about China, your understanding is only superficial. You clearly have no idea what we are actually doing. Take a look at our major technological investment directions: robotics, energy, rockets, AI, computing. The main mission is to go to space—this has all been planned step by step, not blindly investing just to compete with other countries. We spent more than a decade building a powerful energy network so that we won't, like the U.S., disrupt ordinary people's lives when operating AI. Affordable AI modules allow rapid nationwide deployment. A complete industrial chain enables us to produce robots at extremely low costs. A massive number of robots will in turn accelerate AI evolution. This is a comprehensive development strategy. If we win the competition with the U.S., we'll certainly be proud; but even if we lose, it won't affect our country's continued investment—because our goal is not to extract cash from capital markets or create more billionaires. Our goal is to reach space as soon as possible, freeing humanity from the conflicts over Earth's resources.

The long‑term goal is, of course, the realization of communism: unlimited energy (our nuclear fusion technology is planned to generate its first kilowatt‑hour of electricity by 2030), unlimited productivity (robots), and unlimited resources (our space technology is also constantly developing and advancing). What does all this mean?

