snippet.textDisplay:
@bartrammeloo5046 It's worse than that, because the AI doesn't actually think, it just predicts what word comes next.

Which means, unlike the average person, you can convince AI of all manner of nonsense by just feeding it garbage to throw off the prediction algorithm.

Case in point: the average one year old baby has an innate understanding of the concept of object permanence. All of the frontier models do not, and I'd argue LLMs are fundamentally unable to develop it.

